Description: Run and supervise Claude Agent SDK sessions
 Codinian starts and supervises local Claude Code sessions through the Claude
 Agent SDK and puts a GTK window around them: a sidebar of running sessions, a
 transcript pane, tool-call approvals, and the project's git state and issue
 tracker beside them.
 .
 The same sessions are reachable from a phone or a second machine over an HTTP
 server that binds to loopback by default and is intended to be published on a
 tailnet. Approving a tool call runs that tool on this machine, so the bind
 stays closed and every request carries a token.
 .
 The claude-agent-sdk Python package is not in Debian and is therefore not a
 dependency here; install it with pip. Note that the wheel on PyPI bundles a
 317 MB copy of the claude binary, which "pip install --no-binary
 claude-agent-sdk" avoids by building the pure-Python sdist instead.
